# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — protein-design-workshop
# =============================================================================
# What belongs here: anything that's generated, downloaded, per-instance,
# secret, or otherwise should not live in version control. Anything in the
# repo that a contributor edits by hand should NOT be ignored.
# =============================================================================

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Conda ---
.conda/

# --- OS ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
._*

# --- Editors ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# --- Secrets — DO NOT commit ---
# AWS keypairs, env files, and any credentials. If you ever find one of
# these has been committed in history, rotate it immediately.
*.pem
*.key
.env
.aws/

# =============================================================================
# Workshop-specific
# =============================================================================

# --- Per-instance generated by setup.sh ---
# start_app.sh is regenerated on every install with the local CONDA_ROOT and
# absolute paths baked in, so it must not be committed. setup.sh produces it
# at the repo root; an older copy may also live in streamlit_ui/.
start_app.sh
streamlit_ui/start_app.sh

# Setup logs (timestamped, written by setup.sh)
setup-*.log

# --- Workshop run artifacts ---
# These accumulate during workshop runs (per-team PDBs, ColabFold outputs,
# intermediate fasta files). Regenerated on every "Generate & validate" click.
streamlit_ui/inputs/
streamlit_ui/outputs/

# --- Large regenerable artifacts ---
# These typically live under $HOME (not the repo) but if anyone symlinks or
# copies them into the repo tree, defend against accidental commits.
# - msa_cache/   ~10 MB of cached MSAs, repopulated by setup_msa_cache.sh
# - params/      ~3.5 GB of AlphaFold2 weights, downloaded by setup.sh
# - RFdiffusion/ The RFdiffusion repo + ~2 GB of model checkpoints, cloned by setup.sh
msa_cache/
params/
RFdiffusion/

# --- Session notes / handoff docs ---
# Used during development to pass context across sessions. Not source.
handoff/

# Random test files
setup.sh.fullOld

# Local reference files used during development, not source.
# These get inlined into streamlit_ui/app.py (TARGETS functional_residues
# field) — keeping them around as untracked files means git status would
# always be dirty, so ignore them.
appFormat.py
petase_annotations.py
petase_functional_residues.md
zar1_annotations.py
zar1_annotations_extended.py
zar1_functional_residues.md
zar1_functional_residues_extended.md
carrp_annotations.py
carrp_functional_residues.md
gh29_annotations.py
gh29_functional_residues.md
gh29_lane_workplan.md

# Per-instance staging symlinks into ~/rfd-bonus-staging/ (RFdiffusion bonus
# content). Targets are absolute paths under $HOME, so the symlinks would
# break for anyone else — don't commit them.
setup.sh.new
streamlit_ui/app_rfd.py
